---
<div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-white tracking-tighter uppercase mb-8">How it works</h2>
    
    <div class="space-y-8 relative before:absolute before:inset-0 before:ml-5 before:-translate-x-px md:before:mx-auto md:before:translate-x-0 before:h-full before:w-0.5 before:bg-gradient-to-b before:from-indigo-500 before:via-emerald-500 before:to-transparent">
        
        <!-- Step 1: Config -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center justify-between md:justify-normal md:odd:flex-row-reverse group">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-4 border-slate-950 bg-indigo-600 text-white font-bold shrink-0 md:order-1 md:group-odd:-translate-x-1/2 md:group-even:translate-x-1/2 shadow-lg z-10">1</div>
            <div class="w-[calc(100%-4rem)] md:w-[calc(50%-2.5rem)] bg-slate-900 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 shadow-xl">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-indigo-400 mb-2 mt-0">Configure the Rules</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 m-0">The Room Owner sets the boundaries. Want a brutally hard game? Limit the node pool to obscure 90s anime and remove Voice Actors.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2: Build -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center justify-between md:justify-normal md:odd:flex-row-reverse group">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-4 border-slate-950 bg-emerald-500 text-white font-bold shrink-0 md:order-1 md:group-odd:-translate-x-1/2 md:group-even:translate-x-1/2 shadow-lg z-10">2</div>
            <div class="w-[calc(100%-4rem)] md:w-[calc(50%-2.5rem)] bg-slate-900 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 shadow-xl">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-2 mt-0">Phase 1: Build the Trap</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 m-0">Both players get an empty canvas and the allowed node pool. You have X minutes to construct the most complex, misleading path possible between a Start and Target node.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3: Solve -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center justify-between md:justify-normal md:odd:flex-row-reverse group">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 rounded-full border-4 border-slate-950 bg-rose-500 text-white font-bold shrink-0 md:order-1 md:group-odd:-translate-x-1/2 md:group-even:translate-x-1/2 shadow-lg z-10">3</div>
            <div class="w-[calc(100%-4rem)] md:w-[calc(50%-2.5rem)] bg-slate-900 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 shadow-xl">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-rose-400 mb-2 mt-0">Phase 2: Escape</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 m-0">The timer resets and the graphs are swapped. You now have to solve your opponent's web. The first player to successfully connect the path wins the match.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>